# Using an Arduino library
# Level 5 - Advanced
#
# A rainbow on a NeoPixel LED strip, using the Adafruit NeoPixel library straight from Mujard.
# You learn: 'use' with any Arduino library (pinned to a version), calling it, and a cpp: block for plain C++.
# You need: a WS2812 / NeoPixel strip of 8 LEDs: DIN to pin 6, 5V and GND. Long strips need their own 5 V supply.

board uno
use "Adafruit NeoPixel" version "1.12.3"

strip = Adafruit_NeoPixel(8, pin 6, NEO_GRB + NEO_KHZ800)

var hue = 0

at start:
    strip.begin()
    strip.setBrightness(40)        # library calls look just like the library's own examples

every 20 ms:
    hue = (hue + 256) mod 65536    # walk round the colour wheel
    strip.fill(strip.ColorHSV(hue))
    strip.show()

cpp:
    // Anything Mujard can't say yet can be written in C++ here. Mujard doesn't check it, so keep it small.
    static_assert(sizeof(int) >= 2, "int too small");
